  "generated_text": "1. **Count the number of complementary sets where all three cards have the same shape:**\n   - There are 3 shapes (circle, square, triangle).\n   - For each shape, there is only one way to choose all three cards of that shape.\n   - Therefore, there are $3$ such sets.\n\n2. **Count the number of complementary sets where all three cards have the same color:**\n   - There are 3 colors (red, blue, green).\n   - For each color, there is only one way to choose all three cards of that color.\n   - Therefore, there are $3$ such sets.\n\n3. **Count the number of complementary sets where all three cards have the same shade:**\n   - There are 3 shades (light, medium, dark).\n   - For each shade, there is only one way to choose all three cards of that shade.\n   - Therefore, there are $3$ such sets.\n\n4. **Calculate the total number of complementary sets:**\n   - The total number of complementary sets is the sum of the sets counted in each of the above steps.\n   - Total $3 + 3 + 3 = 9$.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{9}$.",
